# A name another system wrote in lower case (roadmap disk-scheduler.md D19;
# tests/posix/names.c, NAMES_LOWERCASE): B's FRAG.TXT made frag.txt on the
# image ('B lowercase'). It is listed as it is and cannot be opened, since
# frag.txt means FRAG.TXT; rename and unlink find it, so it can be put right.
program: idle
define: TEST_POSIX_NAMES
define: NAMES_LOWERCASE
media: B lowercase
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
match: contains
fsck: B
timeout: 120
emulators: bochs
---
names: frag.txt listed as it is (1): 1
names: FRAG.TXT not listed (0): 0
names: frag.txt opened (-1, ENOENT 2): -1, errno 2
names: renamed to two.txt (0): 0
names: two.txt opened (3): 3
names: removed (0): 0
names: done
